# G110 — Travel Planner System

*v2. See `travel-planner.md` for prose: chain-of-edges validation,
two independent invariants (location chain and time chain), tight-
layover as warning, layovers derived from consecutive legs,
span = transit + layover identity.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Vault Trip Planner

[vault-trip-planner @trip-path
    IN ORDER TO
        load a trip, validate its chain invariants
        derive layovers from consecutive legs
        and render the trip with live issue feedback on every edit

    @trip <- [trip[load {path: @trip-path}]]

    @issues   <- [trip[validate {trip: @trip}]]
    @layovers <- [trip[layovers {trip: @trip}]]

    [ui[render-trip
        {title: @trip:title,
         legs: @trip:legs,
         layovers: @layovers,
         issues: @issues,
         metrics: {
            span:       [trip[total-span-ms     {trip: @trip}]],
            in-transit: [trip[in-transit-ms     {trip: @trip}]],
            layover:    [trip[total-layover-ms  {trip: @trip}]],
            cost:       [trip[total-cost-cents  {trip: @trip}]]
         }}]]

    sync @user-events {
        edit-leg @idx @new-leg ->
            [trip[replace-leg {trip: @trip, idx: @idx, leg: @new-leg}]]
            @issues <- [trip[validate {trip: @trip}]]
            [ui[refresh-issues {issues: @issues}]]
    }
]

---

## Verb Surface

[trip
    new                    {id, title}
    add-leg                {trip, leg}
    replace-leg            {trip, idx, leg}
    validate               {trip}                ;; -> [Issue]
    layovers               {trip}                ;; -> [Layover]
    total-span-ms          {trip}
    in-transit-ms          {trip}
    total-layover-ms       {trip}
    total-cost-cents       {trip}
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: the chain as a `where` on consecutive pairs

[trip[validate {trip: @trip}]
    IN ORDER TO
        produce one issue per broken invariant
        across per-leg checks and per-pair chain checks
        so the user can fix each issue independently

    @per-leg <- @trip:legs
        where arrive-ms is less than depart-ms
            -> #negative-duration-leg (severity: Error, leg-idx)
        or where arrive-ms is equal to depart-ms
            -> #zero-duration-leg (severity: Warning, leg-idx)

    @per-pair <- @trip:legs paired-with-next as (@a, @b)
        where @a:destination is not @b:origin
            -> #location-mismatch (severity: Error, leg-idx: @b:idx)
        or where @b:depart-ms is less than @a:arrive-ms
            -> #time-conflict (severity: Error, leg-idx: @b:idx)
        or where (@b:depart-ms - @a:arrive-ms) / 60000
              is between 1 and @trip:min-layover-minutes - 1
            -> #tight-layover (severity: Warning, leg-idx: @b:idx)

    @per-leg joined-with @per-pair
]

The two check layers compose but never entangle: a broken leg is
reported even when the chain is also broken, so the user sees both
failures at once rather than fixing them in sequence.

## Distinctive Innate idiom: layovers derived, never stored

[trip[layovers {trip: @trip}]
    @trip:legs paired-with-next as (@a, @b)
    IN ORDER TO
        emit Layover records for every consecutive pair
        where the traveller is waiting at @a:destination
        for @b:depart-ms − @a:arrive-ms milliseconds
]

Editing a leg invalidates any cached layovers silently; rederiving is
the only correct response. Same discipline as G095's lazy formulae
and G109's progress roll-up — derived views over a canonical source.

---

## Demo

[demo
    @t <- [trip[new {id: 1, title: "JFK → SFO → LAX"}]]
    [trip[add-leg {trip: @t,
                    leg: {origin: "JFK", destination: "SFO",
                           depart-ms: 100000000, arrive-ms: 120000000,
                           cost-cents: 30000, mode: "FLIGHT"}}]]
    [trip[add-leg {trip: @t,
                    leg: {origin: "SFO", destination: "LAX",
                           depart-ms: 130000000, arrive-ms: 135000000,
                           cost-cents: 15000, mode: "FLIGHT"}}]]

    -> [trip[validate  {trip: @t}]]   ;; -> []
    -> [trip[layovers  {trip: @t}]]
    ;; -> [{location: "SFO", duration-ms: 10000000}]
    -> [trip[total-cost-cents {trip: @t}]]  ;; -> 45000
]
